 "notes": {
  "height": "~11 m flat-topped wall without cornice: 15 (gate apex ~7 m, wall top at ~1.5x the apex height above the pavement = ~10.6 m), notes P5/L1 (11-12 m); w290678899_1 (south of the gate passage) inherits it.",
  "facade": "e0 = street front north of the gate, u from the north end (112.9,-212.8); the gate itself is the mouth of building passage 722675059 at u ~9-11. From 03 (foreground wall) and 15: three rows of sparse windows: small square bar-grilled windows at ~3 m, hooded grilled windows at ~5 m, cage windows at ~8-9.5 m (hoods and cages are plain grilled windows here; features requested). APR street plaque (white tiles, dark frame) ~4 m north of the recess at ~3.5 m (03, 30); scroll-bracket gate lamp (wall_lantern stand-in) beside the recess at ~3 m (07, 16, 30); downpipe at the north end (15).",
  "tint": "very regular pale grey-white limestone, whiter than anywhere on the square (03, 15, 30).",
  "facade_south": "street front south of the gate (piece w290678899_1 after the passage carve), u from the gate jamb (112.3,-224.8): 03, 16, 30 (small hooded window with a diamond grille right of the recess, cages above), gate lamp on this side too."
 },
